      "output": {
        "decision": "answer",
        "reason": "The evidence fully describes the method: the paper uses Ngram language models (bigrams and trigrams, trained with KenLM with modified Kneser-Ney smoothing) built from two corpora (funny @midnight tweets and news data). Each tweet is assigned a probability by each model; tweets with higher probability under the funny-tweet model are considered funnier, while tweets with lower probability under the news model are viewed as funnier. These probabilities enable relative ranking of humorous statements, supporting pairwise comparison and semi-ranking."
      },
